From 65a9e797b3e11a41c6b8ee5de75bbc9d449ab4be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:30:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Write fragment storage images, draw without a fragment
 function, read x420 as Cr Y Cb

14 and 15 snapshot the framebuffer after the language panel with
inplace_copy_lph: a fragment shader with no colour output that writes a
storage image. Reims refused the draw, so the country panel never drew.
The draw now gets a storage image of its own and leaves the attachments
untouched. A level-0 linear texture of the shader texel width seeds the
image and takes its texels back after the draw.

A render pipeline with no fragment function now draws with an empty
fragment shader and colour writes off, instead of being refused.

Format 543 (ten-bit x420) samples as Cr, Y and Cb like 540 to 542. Both
VideoToolbox kernels that read it, on 15 and 27, swizzle .gbr; the
ten-bit one does it when it stores the sample in a local array, which
was misread as the kernel taking Y, Cb and Cr. On 15 the frames now come
out warm gold instead of teal. 27 hello does not sample 543 in current
boots, and its Golden Gate still is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
